<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lorenzino de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1514">1514</a>–<a href="/years/1548">1548</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Lorenzaccio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lorenzino de' Medici was a member of a junior branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-medici">Medici family</a> who murdered his cousin Alessandro, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, in January 1537. He presented the deed as tyrannicide, but the republican exiles failed to profit from it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a> took power. Lorenzino fled abroad and was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1548 by agents of Cosimo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lorenzino-de-medici.jpg" alt="Lorenzino de' Medici" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scuola fiorentina · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scuola_fiorentina,_medaglia_di_lorenzino_de%27_medici.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
